From smcv at debian.org  Mon Sep  7 23:37:03 2020
From: smcv at debian.org (Simon McVittie)
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2020 23:37:03 +0100
Subject: [R-pkg-team] Bug#969765: r-cran-xopen: Please depend on xdg-utils
 instead of bundling a copy of xdg-open
Message-ID: <20200907223703.GA1679219@espresso.pseudorandom.co.uk>

Package: r-cran-xopen
Version: 1.0.0-2
Severity: normal

While using codesearch to find packages that are still using the deprecated
gvfs-bin commands, I found a copy of xdg-open(1) in r-cran-xopen.

Instead of bundling a private copy of xdg-open, please depend on the
xdg-utils package, which contains the canonical copy of xdg-open, and
search the PATH for xdg-open(1). This would have three advantages:

- Bugs fixed in xdg-utils would automatically be fixed for this
  package too.

- If Debian moves to a reimplementation of xdg-open that contains less
  shell script, r-cran-xopen would automatically use that.

- xdg-utils has (or should have...) the necessary Depends and Recommends
  to make its scripts actually work.

Thanks,
    smcv


